// test_bridge_v1_raisedwater_bigjam_mixed_level3_DEBUG_widerstacks_analytical_softdrop_clog_cylinders_ownertiebreak_50k_statslog_tightboth_gas.prm
// ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// MIRROR of ..._50k_statslog_gas.prm (identical scenario, seed, and step count), with BOTH
// ModelParameters.useTightLayer1 true AND useTightTier1 true (see each flag's own comment below) --
// the COMBINED configuration, after the two isolated runs (useTightTier1-only: fallback rate
// 99.475%->0.468% at step 10000, same grand total; useTightLayer1-only: grand total
// 11,937,407->205,432 at step 10000, a 58x reduction, because it rejects pairs BEFORE they ever reach
// the dispatch at all, invisibly to the per-category counters) showed the two flags act at different,
// non-overlapping stages (Layer 1 before the dispatch is ever entered, Tier 1 after a dispatch-gap
// pair is already inside it). Expectation: Layer 1 cuts the volume first (~205K), then Tier 1 cheaply
// resolves nearly all of THAT remainder too, potentially taking real GJK/EPA calls from the base run's
// ~11.9M down to a few thousand. Run as a SEPARATE job from a SEPARATE cluster checkout
// (mt-dennys-mirror, now free) so it can't race any other run's build or output directories. Compare
// all four runs' [ContactDetectionStats] logs afterward -- specifically the NEW
// cylTier1CheaplyProvedSeparated / boxTightLayer1CheaplyProvedSeparated counters and the resulting
// cylinder-cylinder fallback rate.
//
// 50k-STEP DIAGNOSTIC variant of test_bridge_v1_raisedwater_bigjam_mixed_level3_DEBUG_widerstacks_analytical_softdrop_clog_cylinders_ownertiebreak_gas.prm
// (that file's own 200000-step run, job 4192276, TIMED OUT at step 130000 after a 12.5x per-chunk
// slowdown -- 35.2 steps/sec in the first 5000 steps down to 2.8 steps/sec by step 130000 -- as the
// jam built up). This variant caps timesteps at 50000 (well within the region that run completed
// quickly) and turns on the NEW EvaluationParameters.logContactDetectionStatsPeriodically flag (see
// that field's own comment, SimulationParams.h) so [ContactDetectionStats] -- the existing per-run
// tally of which cylinder-cylinder analytical sub-case (face-face, band-band-parallel, face-band,
// band-band-skewed, face-edge, special-contact, band-edge, edge-edge) or GJK/EPA fallback tier fired,
// previously only ever printed ONCE at end-of-run -- gets printed AND RESET every
// performanceLogFrequency (5000) steps instead, giving 10 successive per-interval snapshots showing
// how the sub-case mix (and the GJK fallback rate) shifts as the jam develops, rather than one
// opaque end-of-run total. Everything else UNCHANGED from that file (itself built on the box version
// -- see its own header for the full derivation chain and Z-height/liquidHeightFactor history).
//
// ORIGINAL (200000-step, no periodic stats) HEADER, for the unchanged derivation history:
// CYLINDERS variant of test_bridge_v1_raisedwater_bigjam_mixed_level3_DEBUG_widerstacks_nogjk_softdrop_clog_gas.prm
// (the box version -- crashed twice with RELEASE-OVERLAP, jobs 4175745/4179445). This session already
// ran two other ablations of that same scenario: SPHERES (analytic contact) completed cleanly all
// 200000 steps; boxes kept but routed through GJK+useContactFilterOwnerTiebreak instead crashed EARLIER
// (step 45724) with a different failure, STALE-PARTICLE-IDX (a fluid/mesa_pd particle-ownership
// desync, not RELEASE-OVERLAP -- see that job's own analysis: a genuine flying-cuboid velocity spike,
// ~7500 LU/step, was observed in the log right at the abort). This variant tests a THIRD shape:
// CYLINDERS (radius 1.38, length 12, axis<1,0,0> -- volume-equivalent to the 12x2x3 box, 71.79 vs 72
// LU^3, the SAME radius/length already used for the toy-trunk scenario's own "secondary" cylinders),
// combined with the STANDARD hybrid contact path (useAnalyticalContactDetection=true,
// usePureAnalyticalCylinder=false -- i.e. NOT forced through GJK the way the box+GJK ablation was, and
// NOT restricted to pure-analytical-only either: cylinder-cylinder contacts still fall back to GJK/EPA
// whenever the analytical Kodam+Guo result flags itself uncertain, same as every other validated
// scenario in this project) plus useContactFilterOwnerTiebreak=true (relevant here because that hybrid
// fallback DOES involve GJK for uncertain cylinder-cylinder pairs, same rationale as the toy-trunk
// scenario's own use of this flag). Question: does a rounder, non-wedging shape (cylinders, unlike
// boxes, only ever touch along a line/point for skew contacts, never face-to-face) avoid the crash the
// way spheres did, while still being a more log-like (elongated) shape than a sphere?
// Everything else (domain, drop height Z=87, liquidHeightFactor=2.5, 270 pieces' aim points/wave
// timing, piers, arches, numSubCycles=20) is UNCHANGED from the box version -- see that file's own
// header (reproduced below) for the full Z-height/liquidHeightFactor/REVISION-1/REVISION-2 derivation
// history, none of which was touched here.
//
// ORIGINAL (box-version) HEADER, for the unchanged derivation history:
// SOFT-DROP variant of test_bridge_v1_raisedwater_bigjam_mixed_level3_DEBUG_widerstacks_nogjk_lowwater_clog_gas.prm
// (job 4169047, COMPLETED cleanly at 150000 steps -- see that file's own history for the full
// 270-box/18-aim-point/15-wave derivation, unchanged here). That run showed boxes visibly flying
// around after release: each box spawned at Z=86 (10 LU ABOVE the deck top, Z=76) while the water
// surface sat around Z~53.7-54.5 (liquidHeightFactor=2.0, plateau) -- a ~32-33 LU freefall through
// open air before impact, producing a hard splash-in that could launch boxes back out. TWO changes
// fix this:
//   1. Drop point moved from Z=86 down to Z=84 (originally tried Z=76, exactly deck-top height --
//      see the REVISION note below for why that was corrected).
//   2. liquidHeightFactor raised 2.0 -> 2.5 (absoluteLiquidHeight ~53.11 vs ~49.11 at baseline --
//      avgParticleDiameter=8.0 LU for this domain, confirmed consistent across the 1.0/2.0/4.0
//      tiers already measured this session: absoluteLiquidHeight = 8.0*(4.1393+liquidHeightFactor)).
//      NOT chosen to preserve free (unsubmerged) flow under the arches (springing line Z=56) the
//      way the earlier "lowwater" tuning was -- this run's goal is softening the drop impact, not
//      arch-scrape testing, so some arch submersion during pileup is an accepted tradeoff here.
// timesteps bumped 150000 -> 200000 (vs job 4169047) to give the jam extra time to develop/hold
// under the new, gentler release given the water level (and therefore backwater dynamics) changed.
// Everything else (domain, 270 boxes' X/Y aim points and wave timing, piers, arches, numSubCycles,
// maxOverlap clamp, no floating spheres/cylinders, useAnalyticalContactDetection,
// useArchTunnelAsMesaPDObject) is unchanged from job 4169047's file.
//
// REVISION 1 (after job 4175745 FAILED at step 77001, RELEASE-OVERLAP hard abort): the first attempt
// used Z=76 (exactly deck-top height) for the drop point, reasoned as safe because it sat ~20+ LU
// above the CLEAN, pre-jam water level (~53 LU). But this scenario deliberately engineers a growing
// jam, and its own backwater rises over the run -- pulled the actual fill-level field at step 76000
// (the last write before the crash) and found water height at the piers had already reached ~72 LU
// (only 4 LU short of the deck top), with height ~57 LU even at the X=40 spawn row itself, both
// still climbing (more release waves fire up to step 131000). A later-wave floater at a shared aim
// point therefore released nearly INTO the rising backwater instead of falling freely through open
// air, never gaining enough separation from its still-nearby sibling before the fixed 9000-step wave
// gap elapsed -- a spawn-point collision, not a "gap too short" problem in the ordinary sense. Z=84
// keeps ~12 LU of clearance above the worst backwater height actually observed (and more before the
// jam matures further), while still meaningfully softening the original Z=86 drop.
//
// REVISION 2 (after job 4179445 FAILED at step 95001, same RELEASE-OVERLAP mechanism): confirmed via
// this file's own [SUBCYCLE-LEFT-RANK]/[VELOCITY-JUMP] diagnostics that the OLDER sibling in this
// collision was NOT flying -- its velocity right before the crash was ~0.006 LU/step, completely
// ordinary. It had simply drifted only ~7 LU in X and ~3 LU in Z from its own spawn point over
// thousands of steps (stuck in the same congested backwater the jam itself creates), so the next
// wave at that shared spawn point materialized almost on top of it. Z=84's ~12 LU of margin bought
// ~18000 extra steps (77001 -> 95001) before the ever-worsening congestion caught up again -- raising
// Z further only delays this same recurrence, it doesn't fix the underlying mechanism (a floater that
// never clears its own spawn point no matter how much fall distance it's given). Bumped Z=84 -> 87
// (a further small margin increase) to push this recurrence later still, while a real fix (per-wave
// spawn-point jitter, so consecutive releases can never geometrically overlap regardless of drift) is
// still on the table if this recurs again.
// ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


BlockForestParameters
{
   cellsPerBlock                 < 32, 20, 15 >;
   periodicity                   < 1, 0, 0 >;
   loadSnapshot                  false;
   storeSnapshot                 true;
   snapshotFrequency             10000;
   snapshotBaseFolder            snapshots;
}

DomainParameters
{
   domainSize         <128, 60, 90>;
   wavePeriods        1;
   liquidHeightFactor 2.5;  // SOFT-DROP variant -- see this file's own header; absoluteLiquidHeight~53.11
   floorHeightFactor  4.1393;
   initialAmplitude   0;
}

PIDParameters
{
   targetMeanVelocityMagnitude 0.01;
   proportionalGain            2e-4;
   derivativeGain              1e-6;
   integralGain                2e-4;
   maxRamp                     1e-4;
   minActuatingVariable        0;
   maxActuatingVariable        1e-3;
}

PhysicsParameters
{
   enableWetting     false;
   // 50000 (down from 200000): this run is a diagnostic, not a completion attempt -- see this file's
   // own header. The earlier 200000-step cylinder run (job 4192276) TIMED OUT at step 130000 with a
   // 12.5x per-5000-step slowdown over the run (35.2 -> 2.8 steps/sec) as the jam built up; 50000
   // steps is well within the region that run completed in a few thousand seconds, giving several
   // clean periodic [ContactDetectionStats] snapshots without an all-day wall-clock budget.
   timesteps         50000;
   Re                3100;
   Fr                1.31;
   We                15.6188;
   useHardcodedUnits true;
   // no gravityOverride -- dynamically computed gravity
}

ParticleParameters
{
   inFileName spheres_out.dat;
   bedCopiesInX 1;
   bedCopiesInY 1;
   densityRatio 2.55;
   fixingHeightFactor 1.5;
   frictionCoefficient 0.5;
   restitutionCoefficient 0.3; // wet/waterlogged wood-wood -- these are floating logs, soaked, not dry timber
   numSubCycles 20; // dropped from 40: the formal DEM spring-stability bound (Delta_t_DEM < 2*pi*sqrt(m/k_n),
                     // see LinearSpringDashpot::setStiffnessAndDamping) is cleared by ~2400x margin at 40 and
                     // still ~1200x at 20 -- our crash family (unclamped boxBoxSAT overlap growth, ghost-sync
                     // desync) was never actually caused by insufficient sub-cycling resolution, so this is
                     // testing whether 20 behaves identically to 40 while halving DEM compute cost.
   useLubricationCorrection true;
   useNoSlipParticles false;
   useParticleBed false;
}

// DEM bodies matching the BodyBC piers exactly (BodyBC is LBM-only -- floaters need a real mesa_pd
// body to collide with, and nothing else creates one). 4 cylinders (the piers' round end-caps,
// radius 5) + 2 boxes (the connecting box between them, halfExtents = half of X=61-67/Y=10-20-or-
// 40-50/Z=0-76). center Z is cosmetic (CylindricalBoundary is infinite along its axis).
CylinderPillars
{
   CylinderPillar { center < 61, 15, 38 >; radius 5; }
   CylinderPillar { center < 67, 15, 38 >; radius 5; }
   CylinderPillar { center < 61, 45, 38 >; radius 5; }
   CylinderPillar { center < 67, 45, 38 >; radius 5; }
}

Pillars
{
   Pillar { center < 64, 15, 38 >; halfExtents < 3, 5, 38 >; }
   Pillar { center < 64, 45, 38 >; halfExtents < 3, 5, 38 >; }
}

// One entry per arch, matching the BodyBC arch cylinders below exactly (center Y/Z, radius).
// xMin/xMax DELIBERATELY set to the piers' own straight-box span (61..67).
ArchTunnels
{
   ArchTunnel { center < 0, 5, 56 >;  radius 5;  xMin 61; xMax 67; deckTopZ 76; }  // left arch
   ArchTunnel { center < 0, 30, 56 >; radius 10; xMin 61; xMax 67; deckTopZ 76; }  // central arch
   ArchTunnel { center < 0, 55, 56 >; radius 5;  xMin 61; xMax 67; deckTopZ 76; }  // right arch
}

